[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m (`/Users/najmiraihan/Developer/orch-go/README.md`) documenting the [39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m`orch` CLI commands, usage patterns, and the three supported coding [39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229magents (`agy`, `command-code`, `copilot`), adhering strictly to the [39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mconstraint of not modifying any Go source files.[39m                      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m---[39m                                                                   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m## 1. Scope & Constraints[39m                                             [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- **Target File**: `README.md` (root directory).[39m                      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- **Zero Go Changes**: Do not touch or modify any `*.go` files.[39m       [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- **Accuracy**: Base documentation directly on actual implementation [39m [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229min `main.go`, `agent.go`, and `build.go`.[39m                             [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- **Tone & Style**: Direct, clean, minimal (Ponytail style).[39m          [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m---[39m                                                                   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m## 2. Content Structure for `README.md`[39m                               [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m### 2.1 Header & Overview[39m                                             [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- What `orch` is: A minimal Go CLI orchestrator that runs coding [39m     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229magents in real pseudo-terminals (PTYs), preserving native terminal UIs[39m[49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m and interactive permission prompts verbatim.[39m                         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- Key philosophy:[39m                                                     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m  - Real PTY allocation and raw mode terminal handling.[39m               [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m  - Zero permission bypass: does not pass [39m                            [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m`--dangerously-skip-permissions`, `--yolo`, `--auto-accept`, [39m         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m`--trust`, etc.[39m                                                       [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m  - Sequential execution: agents run one after another, each owning [39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mthe terminal.[39m                                                         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m### 2.2 Supported Agents[39m                                              [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mDocument the three supported agents and their CLI integrations:[39m       [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m1. **`agy`**: Google Antigravity CLI (native terminal UI).[39m            [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Binary: `agy`[39m                                                    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Prompt flag: `--prompt-interactive <text>`[39m                       [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Continue flag: `--continue`[39m                                      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m2. **`command-code`**: Command Code coding agent.[39m                     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Binary: `command-code`[39m                                           [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Prompt: Positional argument[39m                                      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Continue flag: `--continue`[39m                                      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Denied flags: `--trust`, `-t`[39m                                    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m3. **`copilot`**: GitHub Copilot CLI.[39m                                 [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Binary: `copilot`[39m                                                [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Prompt flag: `--interactive <text>`[39m                              [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Continue flag: `--continue`[39m                                      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- Common denied flags across all agents: [39m                             [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m`--dangerously-skip-permissions`, `--yolo`, `--auto-accept`, [39m         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m`--tools-all`, `--permission-mode auto-accept|accept-all`, `--mode [39m   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229maccept-edits`.[39m                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m### 2.3 Installation & Building[39m                                       [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- Prerequisites: Go 1.22+, macOS (Darwin PTY implementation), agent [39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mbinaries on `$PATH`.[39m                                                  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m- Build instructions:[39m                                                 [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m  ```sh[39m                                                               [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m  go build -o orch .[39m                                                  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m  ```[39m                                                                 [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m### 2.4 CLI Commands Reference[39m                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mDocument syntax, options, and behavior for all commands:[39m              [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m1. **`orch list` (alias: `orch ls`)**[39m                                 [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Lists registered agents, their installation status on `$PATH`, [39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mand descriptions.[39m                                                     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m2. **`orch run <agent> [agent...] [flags]`**[39m                          [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Runs one or more agents sequentially in the current terminal.[39m    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Flags:[39m                                                           [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     - `-C, --dir <path>`: Working directory for agents (default: [39m    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mcurrent directory).[39m                                                   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     - `-c, --continue`: Resume each agent's most recent session.[39m     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     - `-p, --prompt <text>`: Initial prompt to start the session [39m    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229minteractively.[39m                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     - `-- <args...>`: Raw pass-through flags handed to the agent [39m    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m(single-agent invocations only; permission-bypass flags strictly [39m     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mblocked).[39m                                                             [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Behavior: If an agent exits non-zero, execution halts immediately[39m[49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m and `orch` exits with that status code.[39m                              [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m3. **`orch build "<task>" [flags]`**[39m                                  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Automated multi-agent lifecycle orchestrating `agy` and [39m         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m`command-code`:[39m                                                       [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     1. Stage 1: `agy` plans the task.[39m                                [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     2. Stage 2: `command-code` reviews the plan.[39m                     [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     3. Stage 3: `agy` implements the task based on plan and review.[39m  [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     4. Stage 4: `command-code` reviews implementation (repeats [39m      [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mfix/review loop up to 3 cycles until `VERDICT: APPROVED`).[39m            [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     5. Final Stage: Runs verification (`gofmt`, `go vet ./...`, `go [39m [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mtest ./...`).[39m                                                         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Flags:[39m                                                           [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m     - `-C, --dir <path>`: Repository directory where agents work [39m    [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m(default: current directory).[39m                                         [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Artifacts: Stored under `.orch/<timestamp>/` containing Markdown [39m[49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229mdocuments (`*-plan.md`, `*-review.md`, etc.) and raw terminal logs [39m   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m(`*.log`).[39m                                                            [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m4. **`orch version`** (`-v`, `--version`)[39m                             [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Prints version (`orch 0.1.0`).[39m                                   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m5. **`orch help`** (`-h`, `--help`)[39m                                   [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m   - Displays CLI usage and flag help.[39m                                [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m                                                                        [49m
[48;2;45;43;85m  [38;2;229;229;229m---[39m                                                                   [49m
